"Software"), including copyrightable portions of those materials and modified
versions of them. It applies only to rights the relevant copyright holder is
entitled to grant. Third-party materials are addressed in section 6.

"Commercial Offering" means a product or service offered or supplied to third
parties for payment, subscription fees, license fees, advertising revenue, or
other monetization. It includes free tiers, features, components, and bundled
items of an otherwise monetized product or service.

"Internal Business Use" means use by an individual or organization, including
its employees and contractors acting on its behalf, as a tool for its own work.
That work may include developing commercial products, performing paid client
work, and preparing commercial deliverables. Internal Business Use does not
include supplying the Software itself to customers as part of a Commercial
Offering or selling customers access to its functionality.

