3. Commercial incorporation and commercialization are restricted

Without a separate written commercial license from the relevant copyright
holder or holders, you must not:

(a) Sell, license for a fee, rent, or otherwise monetize the Software itself,
    any copyrightable portion of it, or a modified version of it.
(b) Incorporate, embed, bundle, link, copy, or adapt the Software or any
    copyrightable portion of it into a Commercial Offering. This applies even
    if the Software is only a small component, has been renamed, or has been
    substantially modified.
(c) Make the Software or a modified version available to third parties as a
    commercial hosted, managed, software-as-a-service, or similar offering.
    This includes charging for access to its functionality or monetizing that
    access through advertising or inclusion in another Commercial Offering.
(d) Distribute the Software or a modified version as a free component or
    free tier of a Commercial Offering in order to avoid these restrictions.

Using the Software as a tool to create or support a separate commercial product
is permitted. Including the Software's protected code or other protected
materials in that product is not permitted under this license.

For example, a business may use Prompt Builder to prepare prompts for a paid
application or client project. It may not copy Prompt Builder's template parser
into that paid application, sell a renamed fork, or offer a paid hosted version
without a separate written commercial license.

